and ``_kv_free_metadata_only`` below.\n        self._kv_active_count: Dict[int, int] = {}   # == hwm per layer\n        self._kv_free_heap: Dict[int, list] = {}     # min-heap of free slots\n        self._kv_free_slots: Dict[int, set] = {}     # membership (lazy-delete)\n        # Signals dual_memory_loader.kv.free_slot that this compressor's free path touches no\n        # GPU/host pool memory, so the pre-free decode-stream sync is unneeded.\n        self._kv_free_metadata_only = True\n        # Decode staging H2D: copy only the occupied (live) slot RUNS in\n        # [0:hwm), batching them into one cudaMemcpyBatchAsync so holes\n        # (freed-not-yet-realloc'd slots — possible whenever frees outpace\n        # allocs, e.g. a drain phase) aren't transferred.  ``free_set`` is the\n        # sparse bitarray of holes, so runs come from a membership split (no\n        # sort).  Below this hole count a single [0:hwm] copy is cheaper than\n        # the scan, so we skip it (env-tunable; 0 = always batch).\n        self._decode_hole_threshold = int(os.getenv(\n            \"TIERED_SERVE_KV_DECODE_HOLE_THRESHOLD\", \"32\"))\n        self._batch_ext = None      # cached zipserv_ext for batch_memcpy\n        # Decode-arg CPU-dispatch trims (the per-layer Python/torch op count is\n        # what stalls before_replay — ~20 dispatches x n_layers showed up as\n        # ~2 ms of forward-thread CPU before the blob batchmemcpy in nsys):\n        #  - grid sizing uses STATIC caps (M_b / exc_cap) instead of four\n        #    per-layer pinned .max() reductions; the per-block device arrays\n        #    still bound each block's work in-kernel.\n        #    TIERED_SERVE_KV_DECODE_VALIDATE=1 restores the exact maxes\n        #    (tighter grids + full corrupt-meta detection) for debugging.\n        #  - the block-id vector is identical for every layer of a step, so\n        #    its CPU tensor + device upload are cached step-level\n        #    (content-keyed) and reused by the rem